# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Secrets / local env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Claude Code: `.claude/settings.json` (the shared hooks) is committed; personal permissions are not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local working store — durable state is the committed JSON/CSV snapshots, NOT the binary DB.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Everything under data/ is git-ignored — the working DB, the EOD cache, and the LICENSED manual
# CIQ exports (data/manual/ciq/, never committed) — EXCEPT (a) the durable JSONL snapshots,
# (b) the DERIVED per-ticker dossiers (extracted {value, source_ref} facts + synthesis + verbatim
# PUBLIC 10-K phrases, NOT reproduced licensed CIQ), and (c) data/graph_coverage.json (the EDGAR-
# 10-K-derived exposure map — verbatim PUBLIC 10-K phrases + the relationship-TYPE taxonomy only,
# never CIQ workbook data). All three are committed provenance for the authed deploy; the per-run
# llm_call.log is a regenerated debug artifact and stays ignored.
# NOTE (2026-10-22): the repo is PUBLIC by operator decision and these STAY committed — un-ignoring
# them now would not un-publish history (docs/records/2026-10-22-repo-made-public.md).
data/*
!data/snapshots/
!data/dossiers/
data/dossiers/*/llm_call.log
!data/graph_coverage.json
# (d) data/followed.json — the operator's FOLLOW decisions (TICKER → why the cap band does not
# apply to this name). Hand-authored judgement, neither derived nor licensed: it must be committed
# and diffable, because it is the standing record of which out-of-band names the fund covers and
# why, and the reason it carries is printed in each such dossier's own main body.
!data/followed.json
# Monitor: the dated book history + the benchmark assignments. DERIVED analysis (returns and
# excess-vs-benchmark computed from the committed ledger and EOD closes), and the AUDIT TRAIL of
# how the book was marked on each date — a spread nobody can re-read is not evidence. Small,
# diff-able, no licensed workbook content.
!data/monitor/
!data/scan_history/
# (e) data/calls/ — the CALLS TAPE corpus, one directory per X account. Third-party PUBLIC posts
# (text, engagement counts, cashtags), the machine + hand labels over them, and the fetched Polygon
# bars. No licensed workbook content and no credential; committed so the authed deploy serves it
# without a build step, and so the hand labels — the ground truth this tool exists to grow — are
# diffable. `bars/` is regenerable from Polygon but committed for the same reason snapshots are:
# the page is a static mirror and fetches nothing itself.
!data/calls/

# Frontend — generated mirrors from frontend/build.py. frontend/snapshots/ stays ignored (regenerate
# via build.py). frontend/dossiers/ IS committed — the pre-built DERIVED dossier.json the authed
# viewer fetches, so a static serve works without a build step. Raw CIQ in data/manual/ciq stays
# ignored regardless. (If the repo/deploy goes public, frontend/dossiers reverts to ignored.)
frontend/snapshots/
# frontend/theme-intelligence/ IS committed (operator decision 2026-10-13) — the research desk published
# into the app: derived analysis with short source quotes, never article text. Reverts to ignored with
# frontend/dossiers if the repo/deploy goes public.
node_modules/

# THEME FORWARD-VALIDATION ARTIFACTS — COMMITTED as of 2026-08-12, reversing the standing
# "derived, LOCAL-only, never committed" rule for the two per-driver records below. The loose
# `forward_*` filenames and `data/forward/` stay ignored: only the canonical paths are tracked.
#
# WHY THE RULE CHANGED. Stage-4's entire product is a number that accrues over CALENDAR TIME, and
# its inputs existed on exactly one machine — so on any other checkout the accrual could not be
# computed at all. Three themes froze in July 2026 and two passed their 30-day horizon with their
# diagnostics still reading "0 days forward from freeze" for precisely this reason. The
# reconstruction path that closed that gap (#412) works ONLY for hold-none freezes, so the first
# RATIFIED theme would have had no durable record of its BUY leg's entry dates anywhere.
#
#   baskets/  the frozen BUY/AVOID/naive references + per-name entry dates — the measurement's
#             input. Derived analysis: tickers, dates, cohorts, layer labels.
#   ledgers/  the append-only ratification record the basket is DERIVED FROM. The basket says which
#             names are in which cohort; the ledger says WHY, in the analyst's own words, one row
#             at a time. The three July 2026 ledgers were lost to the old rule and their judgment
#             is gone with them — only the conclusion survives, in the mirrors.
#
# Both qualify under the private-repo rule: the analyst's own reasoning plus verbatim PUBLIC 10-K
# phrases with accessions, which `graph_coverage.json` and the theme mirrors already carry. Never
# licensed vendor content. (If the repo/deploy goes public, these revert to ignored with the rest.)
forward_*_ledger.jsonl
forward_*_baskets.json
data/forward/
!data/themes/
data/themes/*
!data/themes/baskets/
!data/themes/ledgers/
# thesis cards (operator-declared, brief Item 1) + economics roll-ups (derived, Item 4) — both
# committed classes, same rationale as the baskets: durable inputs/artifacts, not local staging
!data/themes/thesis/
!data/themes/economics/

# scan-history archive (themes-exposure) — timestamped scan snapshots + manifest. DATA, never
# committed (already covered by data/*; explicit here for fail-closed clarity).
# data/scan_history/ is TRACKED (2026-07-31): it is the immutable archive standing
# behind candidate_themes.jsonl, and while it was ignored the 'never clobber the
# prior harvest' guarantee protected nothing — the only committed cluster file had
# no keeper. Derived from public EOD prices + EDGAR SIC; no licensed content.

# earliness-assay v0 harness runtime outputs — derived, LOCAL-only (already covered by data/*;
# explicit for fail-closed clarity). Cards, the efts velocity cache, and the quarter-snapshot archive.
data/assay/
data/assay_cache/
data/assay_history/
# data-quality scorecard: an EXCEPTIONS source's full card, every name for every check — LOCAL-only
# (already covered by data/*; explicit for fail-closed clarity). The committed snapshot under
# data/snapshots/data_quality/ lists the exceptions and names this file by path and sha256.
data/data_quality_full/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Rendered external packs — regenerable exports, never committed (external-record rule
# archives the MEMO verbatim in docs/ic/; the pack itself is a render of committed data).
out/
